<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    arcfox common framework overlay: IMS / VoLTE / VoWiFi platform availability.

    AOSP defaults all three to false (frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/
    config.xml). With config_device_volte_available=false, ImsManager's
    isVolteEnabledByPlatform() returns false, updateVoiceCellFeatureValue logs
    "available = false", reevaluateCapabilities calls turnOffIms(), and
    GsmCdmaPhone then logs useImsForCall=false for EVERY call. No call ever
    enters the IMS path and IMS voice never registers. Measured before this
    change: handleImsConnected occurred ZERO times in the entire log, only
    handleImsUnregistered with CODE_REGISTRATION_ERROR.

    This is not cosmetic. 2G/3G networks are being switched off in many
    countries; without VoLTE this device eventually cannot place a voice call at
    all, because there is no circuit-switched fallback left to drop to.

    PROVEN on the device before shipping, using the debug shortcut ImsManager
    honours ahead of these resources:
        setprop persist.dbg.volte_avail_ovr 1
        setprop persist.dbg.wfc_avail_ovr 1
    then a reboot. Result: "handleImsRegistered: onImsMmTelConnected
    imsTransportType=WWAN" for the first time in this port's history, the VoLTE
    and Wi-Fi calling toggles appeared in Settings, and an ORDINARY call
    (isEmergency=false) ran with useImsForCall=true over an ImsPhoneConnection
    with ZERO notifySrvccState events. It stayed on VoLTE for the whole call
    instead of dropping to circuit-switched.

    Values match stock, which sets all three true in
    vendor/overlay/framework-res__auto_generated_rro_vendor.apk.

    WARNING: these are only HALF the gate. ImsManager requires BOTH the platform
    resource AND the carrier config (carrier_volte_available_bool,
    carrier_wfc_ims_available_bool). See
    packages/apps/CarrierConfig/assets/carrier_config_carrierid_1713_Orange.xml.

    VoWiFi additionally needs the IWLAN services bound, which is the second
    block below.

    NOT NEEDED: an ims-type APN. Adding one to vendor/apn/SK.xml was proposed
    and is unnecessary; measured, IMS registers WITHOUT it because the modem
    raises the IMS PDN from its own ORANGE_SVK mcfg.
-->
<resources>
    <bool name="config_device_volte_available">true</bool>
    <bool name="config_device_vt_available">true</bool>
    <bool name="config_device_wfc_ims_available">true</bool>

    <!-- IWLAN service binding, required for VoWiFi (Wi-Fi calling).

         These three default to EMPTY STRINGS in
         frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config_telephony.xml, and nothing in
         device/motorola or vendor/motorola set them. AccessNetworksManager and
         DataServiceManager read them directly to decide which package provides
         the WLAN DataService, NetworkService and QualifiedNetworksService. Empty
         means no provider, so vendor.qti.iwlan is installed on the device but
         never runs (measured: `ps -A | grep iwlan` returns nothing) and the
         WLAN-transport NetworkRegistrationInfo sits at registrationState=UNKNOWN.

         Same "nothing was ever bound" shape as the ImsService in commit 75b2198.

         Values match stock, which sets all three in
         vendor/overlay/framework-res__auto_generated_rro_vendor.apk.

         Note the resources live in config_telephony.xml upstream, not config.xml;
         overlays match by resource NAME, not by file, so declaring them here is
         correct.

         WARNING: this binds a DataService and a NetworkService that have never
         run on this build. If mobile data or WiFi behaves oddly after a flash,
         suspect this first: revert these three strings, keep the VoLTE bools, and
         VoLTE is unaffected because it does not use the WLAN transport. -->
    <string name="config_wlan_data_service_package" translatable="false">vendor.qti.iwlan</string>
    <string name="config_wlan_network_service_package" translatable="false">vendor.qti.iwlan</string>
    <string name="config_qualified_networks_service_package" translatable="false">vendor.qti.iwlan</string>
</resources>
